[{:db/id 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1dfec754-9c19-551c-8df7-102df6435813"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1dfec754-9c19-551c-8df7-102df6435813" :question/id #uuid "1dfec754-9c19-551c-8df7-102df6435813" :question/math-academy-id "q-34636" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -18 \\\\ 8 & 2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 10 & k-32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 10 & k-32\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-2.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-2\\,⟹\\,k=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4437cfd-d611-50b5-a26a-25a34c0f8218"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4437cfd-d611-50b5-a26a-25a34c0f8218" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4437cfd-d611-50b5-a26a-25a34c0f8218" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-711bff2a-6953-5410-bb47-66e0c9bf361e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a676903a-1471-5d07-b4fb-3436e54d4e03" "answer-94b9bad3-ee59-5063-a347-e17815281f18" "answer-a2f39043-eded-58ee-8538-d1b96c3a350b" "answer-711bff2a-6953-5410-bb47-66e0c9bf361e" "answer-caaab5ae-2e33-5881-8499-57baf2a35a93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a676903a-1471-5d07-b4fb-3436e54d4e03" :answer/id #uuid "a676903a-1471-5d07-b4fb-3436e54d4e03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94b9bad3-ee59-5063-a347-e17815281f18" :answer/id #uuid "94b9bad3-ee59-5063-a347-e17815281f18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2f39043-eded-58ee-8538-d1b96c3a350b" :answer/id #uuid "a2f39043-eded-58ee-8538-d1b96c3a350b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-711bff2a-6953-5410-bb47-66e0c9bf361e" :answer/id #uuid "711bff2a-6953-5410-bb47-66e0c9bf361e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caaab5ae-2e33-5881-8499-57baf2a35a93" :answer/id #uuid "caaab5ae-2e33-5881-8499-57baf2a35a93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186342228 :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & k-6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-15.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-15\\,⇒\\,k=15.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186342237 :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 2 & -1 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-6.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-6\\,⇒\\,k=6.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241021 :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=5 \\\\ 3s-t=-5 \\\\ 2s-t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+2t=5 \\\\ t=2 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+2t & =5 \\\\ -s+2(2) & =5 \\\\ -s+4 & =5 \\\\ s & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-1,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186241025 :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t=5 \\\\ -s-8t=-10 \\\\ 4s+14t=-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 4 & 14 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s-3t=5 \\\\ t=3 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s-3t & =5 \\\\ -s-3(3) & =5 \\\\ -s-9 & =5 \\\\ s & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-14,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-14b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-14)\\cdot 3=-42.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a554ac31-b397-5970-b942-0ac30a77ef87" :activity/id #uuid "a554ac31-b397-5970-b942-0ac30a77ef87" :activity/title "Linear Span of Vectors in N-Dimensional Euclidean Space" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048315 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-19ecde81-ba5d-52b8-b7b7-9282a3f95b93" "step-9b5c264f-f673-5283-81e5-4aa5642b7e81" "step-43f3636b-da52-552f-b6cc-fe77773f48fa" "step-70ef282b-5ccd-5b1e-a1f8-1bcffa1e4789" "step-acd92085-628d-5fd7-8ceb-59efc32f4636"] :activity/first-step "step-19ecde81-ba5d-52b8-b7b7-9282a3f95b93" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-19ecde81-ba5d-52b8-b7b7-9282a3f95b93" :step/id #uuid "19ecde81-ba5d-52b8-b7b7-9282a3f95b93" :step/content "question-1dfec754-9c19-551c-8df7-102df6435813" :step/next "step-9b5c264f-f673-5283-81e5-4aa5642b7e81" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9b5c264f-f673-5283-81e5-4aa5642b7e81" :step/id #uuid "9b5c264f-f673-5283-81e5-4aa5642b7e81" :step/content 17592186342228 :step/next "step-43f3636b-da52-552f-b6cc-fe77773f48fa" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-43f3636b-da52-552f-b6cc-fe77773f48fa" :step/id #uuid "43f3636b-da52-552f-b6cc-fe77773f48fa" :step/content 17592186342237 :step/next "step-70ef282b-5ccd-5b1e-a1f8-1bcffa1e4789" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-70ef282b-5ccd-5b1e-a1f8-1bcffa1e4789" :step/id #uuid "70ef282b-5ccd-5b1e-a1f8-1bcffa1e4789" :step/content 17592186241021 :step/next "step-acd92085-628d-5fd7-8ceb-59efc32f4636" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-acd92085-628d-5fd7-8ceb-59efc32f4636" :step/id #uuid "acd92085-628d-5fd7-8ceb-59efc32f46